# Coding Conventions

Purpose: naming, imports, style, and file focus.

## Naming

- Files: `snake_case.dart`
- Classes, enums, typedefs, extensions: `PascalCase`
- Variables, methods, parameters, providers: `camelCase`
- Private members: `_privateName`

## Imports

- Package imports for cross-folder imports; relative only inside the same small folder tree.
- No circular imports.
- Order: Dart SDK → Flutter → packages → project.

## Style

- `const` constructors where possible.
- Small focused widgets; no business logic in widgets.
- Typed models, not maps, for app data.
- No hard-coded route strings, user-facing text, colors, spacing, or repeated formatting. Use design tokens exclusively ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).
- All user-facing text must be localized with concise, clinically appropriate terminology via ARB keys.
- Use `human_friendly_id` in routes, deep links, and user-visible identifiers — not raw database IDs.
- Reuse shared components from `frontend/lib/shared/` before creating feature-local widgets; check the shared catalog first.
- Menus, UI components, and actions must never be visible or accessible to unauthorized users — enforce RBAC+ABAC ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).
- Presentation files must not define private UI copy classes (`_XxxText`) — use `app_en.arb`.
- `*_workspace_page.dart` files should stay compositional; extract widgets when approaching ~800 lines.
- Treat analyzer warnings seriously.

## File focus

| Suffix | Owns |
|---|---|
| `*_page.dart` | page composition |
| `*_controller.dart` | user actions, presentation state |
| `*_state.dart` | UI state shape |
| `*_repository.dart` | domain contract |
| `*_repository_impl.dart` | data coordination |
| `*_dto.dart` | API shape (`snake_case` JSON per [api-contract](../../.cursor/api-contract.mdc)) |
| `*_mapper.dart` | explicit conversion |

